title: ShinyHunters vishing — Legal-Themed Lookalike Domain Patterns
id: c1f07a83-6e52-4b19-8f4d-73ae0c95b216
status: experimental
description: Detects DNS or proxy requests to the legal-themed lookalike domain patterns Okta Threat Intelligence tied to cluster O-UNC-053, the vishing operation that fed the ShinyHunters leak site and later surfaced targets on INCEPTION. Okta observed targeted organizations listed 1 to 28 days after registration of legal-<target>[.]com, legaldept-<target>[.]com, <target>[.]legal and <target>-legal[.]com, with infrastructure often fronted by Cloudflare (AS13335).
references:
  - https://www.okta.com/blog/threat-intelligence/former_shinyhunters_cluster_moves_to_new_inception_site/
  - https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/shinyhunters-resurfaces-after-fbi-arrests-uses-old-pgp-keys-as-proof/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/11/25
tags:
  - attack.t1566
  - attack.t1598
  - attack.t1111
logsource:
  category: proxy
detection:
  selection_lookalike:
    cs-host|re: '(?i)^legal[-.][a-z0-9-]+\.(com|net|org|info|biz|co|io|us|uk)$|^legaldept-[a-z0-9-]+\.|^[a-z0-9-]+-legal\.(com|net|org|info|biz|co|io|us|uk)$|^[a-z0-9-]+\.legal$'
  condition: selection_lookalike
falsepositives:
  - Genuine law firms, in-house legal departments and legal SaaS vendors using legal-prefixed or legal-suffixed domains
  - Marketing and intake domains for legal-services brands
level: medium
